course: dictionary
lesson: 8668
title: Secret: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Secret is a word with three jobs. As a noun, a secret is something you keep hidden and do not tell others. As an adjective, secret means hidden or known by only a few people, like «a secret door». The third meaning is the special way to do something well: «the secret of a good cake».
explain: Context tells you which meaning you need. «Chloe stays polite but stops sharing secrets.» Here a secret is something you keep to yourself, so it is the noun meaning. Ask: could I swap in "hidden thing" and still make sense? If yes, you have the right meaning.
explain: Not all secrets are the same. A good secret, like a surprise party, is fine to keep. «Any secret someone asks you to keep from your parents is a reason to tell them.» A secret that makes you feel scared or unsafe should go to a trusted adult, because «a secret can grow heavier over time».
fact: Secret is a noun (a secret), an adjective (a secret door) and an adverb (secretly).
fact: «Keep a secret» means do not tell it; «tell a secret» means share it; «in secret» means without anyone knowing.
fact: «Top secret» means so private that only a few special people may know it.
fact: A good secret, such as a surprise party, is fine to keep; a bad secret that makes you feel unsafe should be told to a trusted adult.
fact: «Her family had a password, a secret word only family and trusted friends know.»
exercise: «But her family had a password, a secret word only family and trusted friends know.» What does secret mean here? | Something you eat | Very loud | *Known by only a few people | Very old
exercise: «Chloe stays polite but stops sharing secrets.» In this sentence, what is a secret? | A kind of sweet | An unhappy friend | *Something kept hidden and not told | A place to hide
exercise: Which secret is safe to keep? | A secret that gets heavier every week | *A surprise party for your friend | A secret that makes you feel scared | A secret someone asks you to hide from your parents
test: What does «the secret of a good cake» mean? | A very old cake | *The special way to make it well | A cake hidden in a box | A cake nobody likes
test: Which phrase means to share something you know? | *Tell a secret | In secret | Keep a secret | Top secret
exam: «A secret can grow heavier over time because it has nowhere to go; telling a trusted adult usually makes it much smaller.» What should you do with a secret that makes you feel unsafe? | Write it on a chatbot and forget it | *Tell a trusted adult, because sharing it makes it smaller | Keep it hidden forever | Tell everyone at school
